  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "Assuming \\(a\\neq3,\\) \\(b\\neq4,\\) and \\(c\\neq5,\\) what is the value in simplest form of the following expression? \\[\\frac{a-3}{5-c} \\cdot \\frac{b-4}{3-a} \\cdot \\frac{c-5}{4-b}\\]",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(-1\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(1\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(\\displaystyle \\frac{abc}{60} \\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(\\displaystyle \\frac{1}{abc} - \\frac{1}{60}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(\\displaystyle \\frac{1}{60} - \\frac{1}{abc}\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "a",
    "value": "-1"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-10a-2020-p3.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Rewrite the denominator factors as \\(5-c=-(c-5)\\), \\(3-a=-(a-3)\\), and \\(4-b=-(b-4)\\). The expression becomes \\(\\dfrac{(a-3)(b-4)(c-5)}{-(a-3)(b-4)(c-5)}=-1\\). Thus, A is the correct answer.",
      "hints": [
        "Each denominator is the negative of a matching numerator factor",
        "Count the number of negative signs after cancellation"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
